3.2 LLMs for teaching content generation
The inability of existing LLMs to target the generation of more utilizable features in terms of classroom teaching, which tend more toward correct but uninformative content, has prevented existing LLMs from playing a more creative role in this area than previously. Therefore, to enhance the quality of content generated by LLMs, we propose a uniied framework that integrates LLMs, as shown at the top of Figure 1, and introduce two modules: Context Learning and Dynamic Role Setting to handle traditional teaching tasks such as dialogue completion and expert style transfer. The speciic implementation will be discussed in detail in Section 4.
