4 Scenarios and Approaches
In this section, we will thoroughly elaborate on our proposed uniied framework that integrates LLMs to tackle common teaching tasks. This uniied framework initially undergoes Context Learning (including In-Context-Guidance and CrossContext-Guidance) to ensure a comprehensive understanding of the teaching environment and content. Subsequently, by precisely introducing Dynamic Role Settings, the framework provides LLMs with more professional and relevant content output. Based on these two core modules, LLMs can generate results that are highly aligned with teaching tasks through stepwise reasoning. We will delve into the operational modes of two primary tasks within this uniied framework: Teacher-student Dialogue Auto-Completion (Section.4.1) and Expertise Transfer Learning (Section.4.2). This discussion will demonstrate how these tasks synergistically collaborate to generate superior quality teaching materials. Our solution is designed for seamless integration into classroom instruction, not only to empower teachers in enhancing classroom interaction and dynamism but also to ultimately improve teaching quality through the utilization of AIGC.
4.1 Teacher-student Dialogue Auto-Completion
4.1.1 Task Description. In the ield of education, classroom dialogue is regarded as a key link in teaching interaction. It not only promotes students’ thinking and stimulates their learning interest, but also deepens students’ understanding and application of knowledge. However, in the actual teaching process, due to many unforeseen factors such as equipment failures and sudden teacher absences, the continuity of classroom dialogue is often afected, thereby interfering with the overall efectiveness of teaching. To address this issue, we propose a speciic solution - łTeacher-student Dialogue Auto-Completionž. The creation of this teaching scenario stems from a dual focus on continuity and quality of classroom teaching. When unexpected situations interrupt classroom dialogue, in order to ensure the smooth progress of teaching, we envision building an artiicial intelligence dialogue system that can temporarily replace the role of the teacher. This system needs to have the ability to understand and respond to student questions, while also being able to lead the low of classroom dialogue to ensure the coherence and depth of knowledge transmission. This not only can signiicantly improve students’ learning experience, but also make the entire classroom learning environment more active and eicient. Furthermore, it can also produce supplementary teaching materials, such as additional teaching points and case studies, based on existing classrooms, enriching the curriculum and providing diverse perspectives on the subject matter. For students, they can utilize it to obtain any missing teaching content, thus illing their knowledge gaps. This can be particularly useful for revision purposes or for catching up on missed classes. In solving the problem of this task, our goal is not only limited to illing in the blanks of dialogue, but more dedicated to optimize the entire teaching process, so as to fundamentally improve teaching quality. The necessity of this measure is relected in several aspects: First, coherent classroom teaching can better demonstrate the overall picture of knowledge and help students build a systematic and complete knowledge system; Secondly, through high-quality guidance of classroom dialogue, students can more deeply understand knowledge points, expand thinking and improve application ability; Finally, this solution can also provide powerful teaching assistance tools to help teachers more efectively manage classrooms and guide dialogue, thus further improving teaching efectiveness. Based on the above considerations, we hope to achieve the following speciic efects through the łTeacher-student Dialogue Auto-Completionž task: 1) Efectively address the problem of classroom dialogue interruptions caused by accidental events to ensure continuity and stability of teaching; 2) Improve students’ learning participation and thinking depth through the guidance and assistance of an intelligent dialogue system; 3) Provide teachers with a whole new means of teaching support to help them carry out classroom teaching activities more eiciently. Therefore, we clearly deine the task as: given an incomplete dialogue with gaps, generate a complete dialogue content that matches the classroom teaching scenario.
