5 Human Judgement and Automated Scoring of Generated Teaching Content
To better evaluate the text generation quality of our proposed methods, we adopted two methods for evaluation in the tasks of łDialogue Completionž and łExpertise Transfer Learningž. One is to score the coherence of the text through the Large Model (LM), and the other is to distribute questionnaires to obtain human evaluation results. These two methods take into account the objectivity and subjectivity of judging the generated content, which largely avoids signiicant biases and makes the results more reliable.
5.1 Perplexity-based Statistical Evaluation (PPL)
Text generation plays a crucial role in the ield of natural language processing, aiming to generate coherent, accurate, and semantically rich text. In the educational domain, high-quality text generation is essential for efective educational applications. To address this, we propose a metric called Perplexity-based Statistical Evaluation, designed to evaluate the quality of text generated by large-scale educational models. Speciically, we utilize the Perplexity Score (PPL) as its metric, which measures the inverse log likelihood of a sentence in statistical language modeling. In NLP research, PPL is widely adopted to relect the quality of the generated text [14]. The deinition of PPL is described as follows. For a sentence 𨀀 = 𩀀1, 𩀀2, . . . , 𩀀𦀀 , the likelihood of it can be decomposed as the sequential product of the conditional probability of each word as follows:
